    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0068" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">756D.94/42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-03T14:00:00+09:00">August 3, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 3—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>658. In our immediately following telegram 659, August 3, 3 p.m. we report the
                    substance of a communication received from Consul Bruner at Nagoya based upon a
                    conversation with Mr. Arthur Thomas Porghesse<anchor n="7" xml:id="d81-f1"/> who
                    is the subject of the Department’s instruction No. 1845, November 25,
                        1939.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d81-f2"/> Bruner states that Porghesse probably
                    obtained his information from Takehito Chikui who is Director of the Mutsuwa
                    Shokai which is believed to have been established to further the interests of
                    the younger elements in the Japanese Army. This is probably the case as the
                    views expressed in the following report are undoubtedly held by the younger army
                    elements but they are not necessarily shared by the High Command.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d81-f1" n="7" xml:id="d81-f1-content">
                <p>A naturalized American citizen.</p>
            </note>
